{
  "version": 1,
  "_about": [
    "The station estate: source identity on the Cassandra side, display identity on ours.",
    "",
    "Two names per station, on purpose. `source_name` is what the upstream plant calls",
    "it and is the only name that can be used to reason about a Cassandra partition.",
    "`display_name` is what this system shows, in the US wastewater-treatment naming",
    "convention the product uses (the first registered station was already named",
    "'Effluent Pump Station 03', so this continues that convention rather than inventing",
    "one). Display names are deliberately generic - a creek, street or district plus a",
    "standard function - and are not the names of real identifiable facilities, because",
    "attaching one plant's telemetry to another plant's name would misrepresent both.",
    "",
    "`source_uuid` is IDENTITY and is never rewritten. It is the Cassandra `entity_uuid`,",
    "the Cosmos partition key, and the registry's `source_entity_uuid`. A display name is",
    "a label; changing it must never move data. `rename_station` enforces exactly that.",
    "",
    "`pumps_observed` and `feeds` were measured against the local `iwm_data_202507` dump,",
    "not copied from the supplied inventory: 11 of the 16 entities appear there and every",
    "one of their bay counts matched the stated figure exactly. The five marked",
    "\"present_in_dump\": false are in the inventory but not in this dump, so their pump",
    "counts are stated-only and unverified here.",
    "",
    "`feeds` lists the observed `event_value_type` values. This matters more than it looks:",
    "only event 41 carries the `dex` tag map that the dictionary, the mimic layout and the",
    "unit review are all built on. A station seen only on event 104 publishes the envelope",
    "and a per-bay summary and nothing else, so it can never yield instrument-level points.",
    "Four stations have `dex`; the rest do not."
  ],
