  "_field_notes": {
    "pumps_stated": "PC. Verified against Cassandra bay counts for all 11 stations present in the dump; every one matched.",
    "lift_head": "LH. Units NOT confirmed by the plant; metres is the obvious reading of 34-117 but this is not stated anywhere, so it is carried unconfirmed.",
    "discharge_per_pump": "DPP. Units NOT confirmed. Saraswati's 2931.0 is exactly the `dv` observed in its running snapshot, so DPP is per-pump discharge and `dv` reports the achieved value.",
    "rated_power_mw": "RTP. MW.",
    "observed_power_mw": "OBP. MW, and this is the strongest unit evidence in the project: Saraswati's 24.5 equals the ACTIVE_POWER and /pmw measured from its running pump. At kW, 24.5 against a 40 MW rating would be 0.06% of rated.",
    "total_discharge": "TDIS. DERIVED: equals discharge_per_pump x pumps_stated for all 14 rows where both are given, with zero mismatches. Stored for traceability and validated by test, not treated as an independent input.",
    "source_latitude / source_longitude": "LA / LG. The real plant coordinates (17.76-18.91 N, 78.04-79.92 E; Telangana, India).",
    "display_latitude / display_longitude": "PENDING. To be set to a US wastewater-treatment location, matching the display_name convention. Deliberately null rather than invented. NOTE: once set, display coordinates will disagree with the telemetry's real origin, so anything deriving timezone, weather or regulatory context from them would be wrong. Everything is UTC today, so nothing depends on this yet."
  }
}
